WEBVTT

00:00:00.411 --> 00:00:38.773
CHAPTER I THE MOOC MADE AND THE WIFE It was 6 o'clock on a warm April evening, milking time for farmer lodges 80 cows.

00:00:38.833 --> 00:00:49.323
They stood quietly in the dairy, and the milkmaids were all at work.

00:00:49.383 --> 00:00:57.302
They say, Farmer Lodge is coming home with his new wife tomorrow.

00:00:57.362 --> 00:00:59.922
Said one milkmaid.

00:00:59.982 --> 00:01:05.015
Yes, and she's young and pretty.

00:01:05.035 --> 00:01:07.186
I hear.

00:01:07.246 --> 00:01:10.218
A second girl said.

00:01:10.278 --> 00:01:16.492
She looked past her cow to the other end of the dairy.

00:01:16.552 --> 00:01:19.932
There was another milkmaid there.

00:01:19.991 --> 00:01:26.292
A thin, older woman, about thirty years old.

00:01:26.352 --> 00:01:31.164
The first girl looked at the older woman, too.

00:01:31.224 --> 00:01:34.556
I'm sorry for her.

00:01:34.616 --> 00:01:38.207
She said quietly to her friend.

00:01:38.267 --> 00:01:40.278
Oh, no!

00:01:40.338 --> 00:01:42.758
said the second girl.

00:01:42.818 --> 00:01:46.750
That was years and years ago.

00:01:46.810 --> 00:01:53.897
Farmer Lodge never speaks to Rhoda Brooke these days.

00:01:53.957 --> 00:02:02.306
When the milking was finished, the milkmaids left the dairy and went home.

00:02:02.366 --> 00:02:10.739
The thin woman, Rhoda Brooke, did not walk to the village with the other girls.

00:02:10.799 --> 00:02:18.739
She went up the hill behind the farm to a little house near the trees.

00:02:18.798 --> 00:02:28.304
It was a poor house of only two rooms, and the roof did not keep the rain out.

00:02:28.364 --> 00:02:40.209
At the door of the house, the woman met her son, a boy of about twelve, and they went inside.

00:02:40.269 --> 00:02:48.001
I heard something at the dairy today," the woman said.

00:02:48.060 --> 00:02:53.853
Your father is bringing his young wife home tomorrow.

00:02:53.912 --> 00:02:58.484
I want you to go and look at her.

00:02:58.544 --> 00:03:02.166
Yes, mother, said the boy.

00:03:02.186 --> 00:03:05.928
His father married then.

00:03:05.987 --> 00:03:08.152
Yes.

00:03:08.212 --> 00:03:14.106
You can go into town and do my shopping for me.

00:03:14.166 --> 00:03:22.168
And when you see her there or on the road, look at her carefully.

00:03:22.228 --> 00:03:24.368
Yes, mother.

00:03:24.428 --> 00:03:27.149
What is she like?

00:03:27.209 --> 00:03:29.250
I want to know.

00:03:29.310 --> 00:03:31.130
Is she tall?

00:03:31.190 --> 00:03:33.201
Is she short?

00:03:33.261 --> 00:03:38.354
Are her eyes blue or brown or green?

00:03:38.414 --> 00:03:48.302
Look at the color of her hair, the color of her dress, and look at her hands.

00:03:48.362 --> 00:03:57.638
Does she have small white hands or the hands of a milkmaid, a worker's hands?

00:03:57.698 --> 00:04:02.892
You must look at all these things and tell me.

00:04:02.952 --> 00:04:07.501
Yes, mother, the boy said again.

00:04:07.560 --> 00:04:14.072
He took a piece of bread from the table and began to eat it.

00:04:14.132 --> 00:04:22.739
His mother said nothing more, but turned her thin pale face to the open door.

00:04:22.799 --> 00:04:34.160
Her beautiful dark eyes stared out at the trees, seeing and not seeing.

00:04:34.220 --> 00:04:40.475
The next evening was warm and sunny.

00:04:40.534 --> 00:04:48.186
The road from the town to the farm went up and down a number of hills.

00:04:48.246 --> 00:04:55.678
And near the top of one big hill, the boy saw a carriage behind him.

00:04:55.738 --> 00:05:00.900
It was Farmer Lodge with his new wife.

00:05:00.960 --> 00:05:04.834
She was a pretty young thing.

00:05:04.894 --> 00:05:11.709
Much younger than her husband was a sweet, innocent face.

00:05:11.769 --> 00:05:19.676
The boy carried a heavy bag and was happy to stop and stare for a minute.

00:05:19.736 --> 00:05:30.228
The carriage came slowly up the hill, and the boy took a good, long look at the farmer's wife.

00:05:30.288 --> 00:05:35.326
His eyes never left her face.

00:05:35.386 --> 00:05:49.168
The farmer did not look at the boy once, and at the top of the hill the carriage went faster, leaving the boy behind.

00:05:49.228 --> 00:05:56.166
How that poor boy stared at me, said the young wife.

00:05:56.226 --> 00:05:58.830
Yes, my love.

00:05:58.890 --> 00:06:00.581
I saw that.

00:06:00.641 --> 00:06:06.393
The farmer said, is he a boy from the village?

00:06:06.452 --> 00:06:12.744
No, I think he lives with his mother on one of these hills.

00:06:12.804 --> 00:06:15.275
He knows you then.

00:06:15.335 --> 00:06:16.966
Of course.

00:06:17.025 --> 00:06:23.908
And everyone is going to stare at you at first, my pretty gertrude.

00:06:23.968 --> 00:06:26.186
Yes, I know.

00:06:26.246 --> 00:06:30.447
But that poor boy had a very heavy bag.

00:06:30.507 --> 00:06:35.720
Perhaps he wanted us to help him with the bag.

00:06:35.780 --> 00:06:42.784
Oh, these country boys can carry anything, said her husband.

00:06:42.843 --> 00:06:45.996
They do it all the time.

00:06:46.056 --> 00:06:49.974
The carriage went quickly on.

00:06:50.034 --> 00:06:58.162
After a time the boy left the road and went up the hill to his mother's house.

00:06:58.222 --> 00:07:01.344
She was home before him.

00:07:01.404 --> 00:07:08.096
She took the heavy bag from him and began to take the things out.

00:07:08.155 --> 00:07:12.398
Well, did you see her?

00:07:12.458 --> 00:07:18.384
Yes, I had a good look at her on the road.

00:07:18.444 --> 00:07:21.590
And what is she like?

00:07:21.650 --> 00:07:24.051
She's nice.

00:07:24.111 --> 00:07:26.573
Is she young?

00:07:26.632 --> 00:07:29.804
Well, she's older than me.

00:07:29.864 --> 00:07:32.046
Of course she is.

00:07:32.106 --> 00:07:34.588
But is she older than me?

00:07:34.608 --> 00:07:39.581
No, she's younger.

00:07:39.641 --> 00:07:44.474
What color is her hair?

00:07:44.534 --> 00:07:47.632
It's a brown color.

00:07:47.692 --> 00:07:50.649
And her face is very pretty.

00:07:50.709 --> 00:07:53.722
Are her eyes dark?

00:07:53.782 --> 00:08:00.006
No, they're blue, and her mouth is very nice and red.

00:08:00.066 --> 00:08:05.180
And when she smiles, you can see white teeth.

00:08:05.239 --> 00:08:07.582
Is she tall?

00:08:07.642 --> 00:08:11.454
Said the woman, a little angrily.

00:08:11.514 --> 00:08:13.696
I couldn't see.

00:08:13.756 --> 00:08:16.578
She was in the carriage.

00:08:16.638 --> 00:08:29.668
Then tomorrow you must go to church, go early before she and Mr. Lodge arrive and watch her when she walks in.

00:08:29.727 --> 00:08:33.901
Then come home and tell me.

00:08:33.961 --> 00:08:36.604
Very well, Mother.

00:08:36.664 --> 00:08:40.306
But why don't you go and look at her?

00:08:40.366 --> 00:08:41.879
Never.

00:08:41.938 --> 00:08:45.030
I don't want to see her.

00:08:45.090 --> 00:08:49.421
She was with Mr. Lodge, of course.

00:08:49.481 --> 00:08:54.462
Did he look at you or speak to you?

00:08:54.522 --> 00:08:56.534
No.

00:08:56.594 --> 00:09:04.126
The next day the boy went to church and waited and watched.

00:09:04.186 --> 00:09:16.542
When Mr. and Mrs. Lodge arrived, everybody, not just the boy, stared at the new wife with interest.

00:09:16.602 --> 00:09:35.718
When the boy reached home, his mother said, well, she's not tall, she's short, the boy said, ah, said his mother, pleased.

00:09:35.778 --> 00:09:40.369
But she's very pretty, very.

00:09:40.429 --> 00:09:43.875
She had a beautiful white dress on.

00:09:43.935 --> 00:09:48.664
and it made a lot of noise when she moved.

00:09:48.724 --> 00:09:52.488
Mr. Lodge looked very happy with her.

00:09:52.548 --> 00:09:56.742
No more now, said the woman.

00:09:56.802 --> 00:10:01.024
You can tell me more later.

00:10:01.084 --> 00:10:10.982
In the next days, Rhoda Brooke heard more and more from her son about the new wife.

00:10:11.042 --> 00:10:23.055
The boy often saw Mrs. Lodge around the farmhouse, but his mother never saw her, and never went near the farmhouse.

00:10:23.114 --> 00:10:29.256
At the dairy, the other milkmaids talked a lot about the new wife.

00:10:29.316 --> 00:10:36.845
They usually stopped when Rhoda was near, but she heard some of it.

00:10:36.905 --> 00:10:43.786
she remembered everything and forgot nothing.

00:10:43.846 --> 00:11:05.263
And slowly, Rhoda Brooke made a picture in her head of the young Mrs. Lodge, a picture as good, as true, as a photograph.

00:11:05.323 --> 00:11:33.044
Chapter 2 The Dream One night, two or three weeks later, when the boy was in bed, wrote a brook sat by the dying fire in her little house.

00:11:33.104 --> 00:11:38.308
She stared at the fire for a long time.

00:11:38.368 --> 00:11:45.240
But she saw only the picture in her head of the new wife.

00:11:45.300 --> 00:11:52.872
At last, tired from her day's work, she went to bed.

00:11:52.932 --> 00:11:59.808
But the picture of Gertrude Lodge did not go away.

00:11:59.868 --> 00:12:07.850
When Rhoda slept, the young wife was still there in Rhoda's dreams.

00:12:07.910 --> 00:12:15.896
She sat on Rhoda's body in the bed, staring into Rhoda's face.

00:12:15.956 --> 00:12:26.734
Her blue eyes were cold, and with a cruel laugh, she put her left hand in front of Rhoda's eyes.

00:12:26.794 --> 00:12:38.734
There, on the third finger, was her wedding ring and the phantom of Gertrude Lodge laughed again.

00:12:38.794 --> 00:12:47.681
Rhoda turned this way and that way, but the phantom was still there.

00:12:47.741 --> 00:12:59.747
It sat heavier and heavier on Rhoda's body, and now Rhoda could not move.

00:12:59.807 --> 00:13:13.404
Always in her ears was that cruel laugh, and always in front of her eyes was that left hand with its wedding ring.

00:13:13.464 --> 00:13:29.086
At last, half dead with terror, Rhoda suddenly put out her right hand, took hold of the phantom's left arm, and pulled it hard.

00:13:29.147 --> 00:13:36.898
The phantom fell off the bed onto the floor, and Rhoda sat up.

00:13:36.958 --> 00:13:38.900
Dear God!

00:13:38.960 --> 00:13:40.760
She cried.

00:13:40.820 --> 00:13:43.382
She felt cold.

00:13:43.442 --> 00:13:45.894
So cold.

00:13:45.954 --> 00:13:49.257
That was not a dream.

00:13:49.317 --> 00:13:51.798
She was here!

00:13:51.858 --> 00:13:57.002
She could still feel the young woman's arm under her hand.

00:13:57.062 --> 00:14:00.818
A warm, living arm.

00:14:00.878 --> 00:14:08.702
She looked on the floor for the woman's body, but there was nothing there.

00:14:08.762 --> 00:14:21.834
Rhoda Brooke slept no more that night, and at the dairy, early the next morning, she looked pale and ill.

00:14:21.894 --> 00:14:29.504
She could not forget the feel of that arm under her hand.

00:14:29.564 --> 00:14:35.476
When she came home for breakfast, her son asked her.

00:14:35.536 --> 00:14:40.518
What was that noise in your room last night, Mother?

00:14:40.578 --> 00:14:43.790
Did you fall off the bed?

00:14:43.850 --> 00:14:45.841
Noise?

00:14:45.901 --> 00:14:49.413
What time did you hear it?

00:14:49.473 --> 00:14:52.664
About two o'clock.

00:14:52.724 --> 00:14:55.406
But what was it, Mother?

00:14:55.466 --> 00:14:57.367
Something fell.

00:14:57.427 --> 00:14:59.148
I heard it.

00:14:59.208 --> 00:15:01.736
Was it you?

00:15:01.796 --> 00:15:11.229
Rhoda did not answer, and after breakfast she began to do her work in the house.

00:15:11.289 --> 00:15:19.486
At about midday she heard something and looked out of the window.

00:15:19.546 --> 00:15:28.547
At the bottom of the garden stood a woman, the woman from her dream.

00:15:28.607 --> 00:15:34.151
Rhoda stood still and stared.

00:15:34.211 --> 00:15:38.442
The boy came to look out of the window, too.

00:15:38.502 --> 00:15:42.183
Oh, there's Mrs. Lodge!

00:15:42.243 --> 00:15:49.715
He said, she told me, told you, said his mother.

00:15:49.775 --> 00:15:53.006
She looked angry.

00:15:53.026 --> 00:15:55.576
Why did you speak to her?

00:15:55.636 --> 00:15:58.490
I told you not to.

00:15:58.550 --> 00:16:01.564
She spoke to me first.

00:16:01.624 --> 00:16:04.766
I met her in the road.

00:16:04.826 --> 00:16:07.558
When was this?

00:16:07.618 --> 00:16:09.858
Yesterday.

00:16:09.918 --> 00:16:13.050
What did you tell her?

00:16:13.110 --> 00:16:14.872
Nothing.

00:16:14.932 --> 00:16:20.566
She began to talk to me, and then she saw my old shoes.

00:16:20.626 --> 00:16:24.778
She said, Do they keep the rain out?

00:16:24.838 --> 00:16:28.196
And I said, No, they don't.

00:16:28.256 --> 00:16:32.974
But Mother and I have no money for new shoes.

00:16:33.034 --> 00:16:38.546
Then she said, I can give you some better shoes.

00:16:38.606 --> 00:16:42.478
She's bringing them now, I think.

00:16:42.538 --> 00:16:45.540
Perhaps they're in her bag.

00:16:45.600 --> 00:16:48.621
She's very nice, Mother.

00:16:48.681 --> 00:16:53.553
She gives things to lots of people.

00:16:53.613 --> 00:16:58.373
By now Mrs. Lodge was at the door.

00:16:58.433 --> 00:17:05.897
Rhoda wanted to run away, but there was no back door in her little house.

00:17:05.957 --> 00:17:12.322
So she waited, and the boy ran to open the door.

00:17:12.383 --> 00:17:19.618
This is the right house then, said Mrs. Lodge, smiling at the boy.

00:17:19.678 --> 00:17:23.935
And this is your mother, is it?

00:17:23.994 --> 00:17:31.204
The face and body were the same as those of the phantom in Rhoda's dream.

00:17:31.264 --> 00:17:36.078
But there was nothing cruel in this face.

00:17:36.138 --> 00:17:44.536
The blue eyes were warm, and the smile was sweet and kind.

00:17:44.596 --> 00:17:52.760
The young woman took the shoes out of her bag and gave them to the boy.

00:17:52.820 --> 00:17:59.352
She smiled and talked in a warm and friendly way.

00:17:59.412 --> 00:18:04.884
How kind she is, thought Rhoda.

00:18:04.944 --> 00:18:09.678
How young and sweet and innocent.

00:18:09.738 --> 00:18:14.420
Why did I have that bad dream about her?

00:18:14.480 --> 00:18:20.114
She's a friend, not an enemy.

00:18:20.174 --> 00:18:29.050
Two days later, Mrs. Lodge came again, with a new shirt for the boy.

00:18:29.110 --> 00:18:36.206
And twelve days after that, she visited Rhoda a third time.

00:18:36.266 --> 00:18:40.258
The boy was out that day.

00:18:40.318 --> 00:18:44.820
I like walking up here on the hill.

00:18:44.880 --> 00:18:47.802
Mrs. Lodge told Rhoda.

00:18:47.862 --> 00:18:52.641
And your house is the only one up here.

00:18:52.701 --> 00:18:58.199
They talked about the weather and the village.

00:18:58.259 --> 00:19:03.050
Then Mrs. Lodge got up to leave.

00:19:03.110 --> 00:19:06.771
Are you well, Rhoda?

00:19:06.831 --> 00:19:08.462
She asked.

00:19:08.522 --> 00:19:11.002
You look pale.

00:19:11.062 --> 00:19:15.523
Oh, I'm always pale.

00:19:15.583 --> 00:19:17.804
Said Rhoda.

00:19:17.864 --> 00:19:21.815
But what about you, Mrs. Lodge?

00:19:21.875 --> 00:19:24.638
Are you well?

00:19:24.698 --> 00:19:27.540
Yes, I am.

00:19:27.600 --> 00:19:31.271
But there is something.

00:19:31.331 --> 00:19:33.961
It's nothing very bad.

00:19:34.021 --> 00:19:37.392
But I don't understand it.

00:19:37.452 --> 00:19:42.483
She uncovered her left hand and arm.

00:19:42.543 --> 00:19:45.933
There were marks on the arm.

00:19:45.993 --> 00:19:48.984
Yellowy brown marks.

00:19:49.044 --> 00:19:53.024
Like marks made by fingers.

00:19:53.084 --> 00:19:56.452
Rhoda stared at them.

00:19:56.512 --> 00:19:59.180
How did it happen?"

00:19:59.240 --> 00:20:01.411
she asked.

00:20:01.471 --> 00:20:05.792
I don't know, said Mrs. Lodge.

00:20:05.852 --> 00:20:11.462
One night, when I was in bed, I had a dream.

00:20:11.522 --> 00:20:17.254
And then suddenly my arm hurt very badly.

00:20:17.314 --> 00:20:21.694
Perhaps I hit it on something in the daytime.

00:20:21.754 --> 00:20:24.555
But I don't remember it.

00:20:24.615 --> 00:20:26.868
She laughed.

00:20:26.928 --> 00:20:31.404
My dear husband says it's nothing very much.

00:20:31.464 --> 00:20:35.056
And he's right, of course.

00:20:35.116 --> 00:20:37.458
Yes.

00:20:37.518 --> 00:20:40.950
Which night was that?

00:20:41.010 --> 00:20:43.161
Said Rhoda.

00:20:43.221 --> 00:20:46.794
Mrs. Lodge thought for a moment.

00:20:46.854 --> 00:20:50.976
It was two weeks ago today.

00:20:51.036 --> 00:20:54.118
It was two o'clock in the night.

00:20:54.178 --> 00:21:07.668
I remember, because I heard the clock It was the same night, the same hour as Rhoda's dream of the Phantom.

00:21:07.728 --> 00:21:13.573
Rhoda remembered the terror of it and felt cold.

00:21:13.633 --> 00:21:16.382
How can this be?"

00:21:16.442 --> 00:21:20.034
she thought, when Mrs. Lodge left.

00:21:20.094 --> 00:21:22.584
Did I do that?

00:21:22.644 --> 00:21:24.695
But why?

00:21:24.755 --> 00:21:28.786
She is innocent and kind.

00:21:28.846 --> 00:21:31.737
I don't want to hurt her.

00:21:31.797 --> 00:21:35.858
And how can a thing like that happen?

00:21:35.918 --> 00:21:48.779
Only witches can do things like that.

00:21:48.838 --> 00:22:13.654
Chapter 3 The Face in the Glass The days went past and Rhoda Brooke was afraid to meet Mrs. Lodge again.

00:22:13.714 --> 00:22:25.358
She liked her, and did not want to remember the strange dream, or the strange marks on the young wife's arm.

00:22:25.418 --> 00:22:31.040
But she could not stop thinking about them.

00:22:31.100 --> 00:22:36.942
One day they met on the road from the village.

00:22:37.002 --> 00:22:48.812
They began to talk, and after a minute or two, Rhoda said, How is your arm, Mrs. Lodge?

00:22:48.872 --> 00:22:51.874
Is it better now?

00:22:51.934 --> 00:22:55.327
No, it isn't.

00:22:55.386 --> 00:22:57.958
It's worse than before.

00:22:58.018 --> 00:23:01.900
Sometimes it hurts very badly.

00:23:01.960 --> 00:23:06.072
What does the doctor say about it?

00:23:06.132 --> 00:23:08.574
asked Rhoda.

00:23:08.634 --> 00:23:11.898
He doesn't understand it.

00:23:11.958 --> 00:23:19.792
He just says, put the arm in hot water for five minutes, twice a day.

00:23:19.852 --> 00:23:26.183
Well, I do that, but it doesn't help.

00:23:26.244 --> 00:23:30.334
Can I look at your arm?"

00:23:30.394 --> 00:23:32.785
asked Rhoda.

00:23:32.845 --> 00:23:41.838
Once again, the younger woman uncovered her arm, and Rhoda stared at it.

00:23:41.898 --> 00:23:56.704
The arm was thinner and a little withered, and the marks looked more and more like marks made by fingers.

00:23:56.764 --> 00:24:08.806
Rhoda remembered her dream, and the feel of the arm under her hand in just the same place.

00:24:08.866 --> 00:24:15.118
It looks like the marks of fingers, Gertrude Lodge said.

00:24:15.178 --> 00:24:31.123
She tried to laugh My husband says they are a witch's marks, a witch put her hand on my arm, he says, and it's killing the flesh.

00:24:31.183 --> 00:24:36.354
No, no, said Rhoda quickly.

00:24:36.414 --> 00:24:40.746
She felt cold and afraid.

00:24:40.806 --> 00:24:45.767
Don't listen to those old stories.

00:24:45.827 --> 00:24:49.828
the young wife's face was unhappy.

00:24:49.888 --> 00:25:02.962
No, but you see, I think he begins to love me less because of these marks on my arm.

00:25:03.022 --> 00:25:09.214
Men always like their wives to be pretty, don't they?

00:25:09.274 --> 00:25:13.360
Some men do, said Rhoda.

00:25:13.420 --> 00:25:16.246
But don't show him the arm.

00:25:16.306 --> 00:25:18.988
Cover it all the time.

00:25:19.048 --> 00:25:22.909
And then he can't see it.

00:25:22.969 --> 00:25:28.832
But he knows the marks are there.

00:25:28.892 --> 00:25:31.794
Gertrude looked away.

00:25:31.854 --> 00:25:37.022
But Rhoda could see the tears in her eyes.

00:25:37.082 --> 00:25:46.202
I hope your arm is better soon, Mrs. Lodge," she said quietly.

00:25:46.262 --> 00:25:51.394
She said goodbye, and began to walk home.

00:25:51.454 --> 00:25:59.728
She felt sorry for the poor, innocent young wife, and did not want to hurt her.

00:25:59.788 --> 00:26:04.440
But she did not feel sorry for the husband.

00:26:04.500 --> 00:26:09.405
She walked home, thinking about him.

00:26:09.466 --> 00:26:22.574
So, farmer-large, she thought, you loved me once, but then you left me and did nothing to help me.

00:26:22.634 --> 00:26:35.452
You wanted a new, younger and prettier woman for your wife, but she is not so pretty now, is she?

00:26:35.512 --> 00:26:46.256
The next day, Rhoda walked home from the dairy after evening milking at the usual time.

00:26:46.316 --> 00:26:54.270
She was nearly at her house when she saw Gertrude Lodge behind her.

00:26:54.330 --> 00:26:58.312
Rhoda went down the hill to meet her.

00:26:58.372 --> 00:27:01.364
Oh, Rhoda!

00:27:01.424 --> 00:27:03.644
Called Gertrude.

00:27:03.704 --> 00:27:08.051
I wanted to see you, to ask you.

00:27:08.111 --> 00:27:16.583
Her face was pale and worried, and she held her left arm with her other hand.

00:27:16.643 --> 00:27:24.450
Somebody told me, she said, about a man at Eggedon Heath.

00:27:24.510 --> 00:27:37.538
They don't know his name, but they say he is a famous wise man, and can help people with things like this.

00:27:37.598 --> 00:27:46.394
She looked down at her left arm, and then looked at Rhoda, with hope in her eyes.

00:27:46.454 --> 00:27:52.300
They say, you know about him, this wise man.

00:27:52.360 --> 00:27:54.872
Do you know his name?

00:27:54.933 --> 00:27:58.806
Perhaps they mean Mr. Trendel.

00:27:58.866 --> 00:28:03.687
Rhoda said, slowly, she felt ill.

00:28:03.747 --> 00:28:10.906
This man, Trendle, people said, could do many strange things.

00:28:10.966 --> 00:28:14.577
He could understand dreams.

00:28:14.637 --> 00:28:19.048
He could drive phantoms out of houses.

00:28:19.108 --> 00:28:23.230
He could stop the work of witches.

00:28:23.290 --> 00:28:28.141
I am not a witch, she thought.

00:28:28.201 --> 00:28:30.412
I am not.

00:28:30.472 --> 00:28:35.236
I do not believe in these things.

00:28:35.297 --> 00:28:39.001
Dertrude watched her.

00:28:39.062 --> 00:28:43.014
You know him, she said.

00:28:43.074 --> 00:28:46.346
I can see it in your face.

00:28:46.406 --> 00:28:51.328
Of course, I don't believe in wise men.

00:28:51.388 --> 00:28:53.430
What can they do?

00:28:53.490 --> 00:28:59.462
But, well, I can just go and see him.

00:28:59.522 --> 00:29:02.889
Is it far to his house?

00:29:02.949 --> 00:29:10.429
Yes, about five miles, said Rhoda.

00:29:10.489 --> 00:29:14.092
Well, I must walk there.

00:29:14.152 --> 00:29:18.204
I cannot tell my husband about this.

00:29:18.264 --> 00:29:23.328
Can you come with me, Rhoda, to show me the way?

00:29:23.388 --> 00:29:26.561
Perhaps tomorrow afternoon?

00:29:26.621 --> 00:29:29.262
Oh, no, it's...

00:29:29.322 --> 00:29:30.564
I...

00:29:30.624 --> 00:29:32.366
Rhoda began.

00:29:32.426 --> 00:29:33.976
Please.

00:29:34.036 --> 00:29:36.468
said Gertrude.

00:29:36.528 --> 00:29:41.470
And in the end, Rhoda could not say no.

00:29:41.530 --> 00:29:48.765
Mrs. Lodge was good and kind, and she needed a friend's help.

00:29:48.825 --> 00:29:55.610
But perhaps a wise man could see into people's dreams.

00:29:55.670 --> 00:30:04.834
Rhoda did not want to meet this man, Trendel, and she was afraid.

00:30:04.894 --> 00:30:19.326
The next afternoon, she met Gertrude by the trees near her house, and they began the long walk across the hills to Eggedon Heath.

00:30:19.386 --> 00:30:28.507
It was a cold day, and the sky above the hills was dark and unfriendly.

00:30:28.567 --> 00:30:33.538
They found Mr. Trendel's house outside the village.

00:30:33.598 --> 00:30:47.912
He was at home when they arrived, He was an old man with grey hair, and he looked long and hard at Rhoda when he saw her.

00:30:47.972 --> 00:30:55.534
Mrs. Lodge told him about her arm, and he looked at it carefully.

00:30:55.594 --> 00:30:57.335
No.

00:30:57.395 --> 00:31:02.196
Doctors can't do anything for this.

00:31:02.256 --> 00:31:09.158
He said, this is the work of an enemy.

00:31:09.218 --> 00:31:12.398
Rhoda moved away a little.

00:31:12.458 --> 00:31:14.118
An enemy?

00:31:14.178 --> 00:31:16.260
What enemy?

00:31:16.320 --> 00:31:18.810
asked Mrs. Lodge.

00:31:18.870 --> 00:31:24.683
I don't know, said the wise man looking at her.

00:31:24.743 --> 00:31:28.454
But perhaps you do.

00:31:28.514 --> 00:31:32.576
I can show the person to you.

00:31:32.636 --> 00:31:36.338
Do you want me to do that?

00:31:36.398 --> 00:31:39.891
Yes, said Gertrude.

00:31:39.951 --> 00:31:42.682
Yes, please show me."

00:31:42.742 --> 00:31:54.386
Mr. Trandall took Gertrude into another room, but the door was open and Rhoda could see into the room.

00:31:54.446 --> 00:32:01.358
The wise man took an egg and did something to it.

00:32:01.418 --> 00:32:10.295
Then he put a glass of water on the table and carefully broke the egg open.

00:32:10.355 --> 00:32:25.026
The white of the egg went down into the water, changing to a milky white colour and moving slowly round and round.

00:32:25.086 --> 00:32:30.643
He put the glass in front of Gertrude.

00:32:30.703 --> 00:32:35.850
Look down into the water.

00:32:35.910 --> 00:32:40.672
He said, look for a face.

00:32:40.732 --> 00:32:44.954
Gertrude stared down into the water.

00:32:45.014 --> 00:32:48.928
Do you see a face?

00:32:48.988 --> 00:32:53.120
The wise man asked quietly.

00:32:53.180 --> 00:32:59.229
Gertrude whispered something, but Rhoda could not hear.

00:32:59.289 --> 00:33:02.556
She turned away from the door.

00:33:02.616 --> 00:33:10.007
When Mrs. Lodge came out, her face was pale, paler than rotors.

00:33:10.067 --> 00:33:18.468
Mr. Trendel closed the door behind her, and the two women began to walk home.

00:33:18.529 --> 00:33:23.719
But things were not the same between them.

00:33:23.779 --> 00:33:28.546
Did he ask for money?

00:33:28.606 --> 00:33:31.474
Rhoda said quietly.

00:33:31.534 --> 00:33:34.426
Oh no, nothing.

00:33:34.486 --> 00:33:39.670
He did not want a penny, said Gertrude.

00:33:39.731 --> 00:33:42.933
And what did you see?

00:33:42.994 --> 00:33:45.084
asked Rhoda.

00:33:45.144 --> 00:33:47.176
Nothing.

00:33:47.236 --> 00:33:50.939
I don't want to speak about it.

00:33:50.999 --> 00:33:55.532
Gertrude did not look at Rhoda.

00:33:55.592 --> 00:34:06.888
her pretty young face looked ten years older and was now more like the face of the phantom in Rhoda's dream.

00:34:06.948 --> 00:34:11.112
They did not speak for a long time.

00:34:11.172 --> 00:34:21.387
Then Gertrude said suddenly, did you want me to come here and see this wise man?

00:34:21.448 --> 00:34:23.998
How strange of you.

00:34:24.058 --> 00:34:26.636
No, I didn't.

00:34:26.696 --> 00:34:31.768
But now I am not sorry we came.

00:34:31.827 --> 00:34:38.965
For the first time since her dream, Rhoda felt a little pleased.

00:34:39.026 --> 00:34:43.640
Life was cruel, she thought.

00:34:43.700 --> 00:34:49.425
And Gertrude Lodge must learn that lesson too.

00:34:49.485 --> 00:34:58.108
On the long walk home, they did not speak again about their visit to the wise man.

00:34:58.168 --> 00:35:07.112
But other people did, and whispered stories about it in all the farms and dairies.

00:35:07.172 --> 00:35:21.992
Mrs. Lodge could no longer use her withered arm to do anything, and people began to put the word which in front of the name Rhoda Brooke.

00:35:22.052 --> 00:35:50.494
Rhoda said nothing to anybody about the phantom of her dream, but her face got thinner and paler, and in the spring she and her boy left their house and went away into the hills in the west.

00:35:50.554 --> 00:36:11.300
Chapter 4 The Cure for a Curse Six years went past, and Mr. and Mrs. Lodge's married life was not happy.

00:36:11.360 --> 00:36:16.752
The farmer said little, and did not often smile.

00:36:16.812 --> 00:36:27.332
His wife had a withered arm, and there were no children to call him father, and to run laughing around the farmhouse.

00:36:27.392 --> 00:36:34.454
He thought of Rhoda Brooke and her son, his son.

00:36:34.514 --> 00:36:40.835
But that was the past, and he could not change it now.

00:36:40.895 --> 00:36:50.970
Gertrude Lodge was a different woman too, She was only 25, but she looked older.

00:36:51.031 --> 00:36:59.439
Once a happy smiling woman, she was now sad and worried all the time.

00:36:59.499 --> 00:37:08.232
She loved her husband, but he no longer loved her, and she knew it.

00:37:08.292 --> 00:37:15.900
six years of married life, and only a few months of love.

00:37:15.960 --> 00:37:18.782
She sometimes whispered.

00:37:18.842 --> 00:37:22.554
Her left arm was no better.

00:37:22.614 --> 00:37:29.536
She tried one thing after another, but nothing helped it.

00:37:29.596 --> 00:37:36.592
Some of the things were a little strange, and her husband did not like them.

00:37:36.652 --> 00:37:42.244
You think too much about your arm," he said.

00:37:42.304 --> 00:37:48.435
You need somebody to talk to, somebody to be around the house.

00:37:48.495 --> 00:37:52.236
At one time there was a boy.

00:37:52.296 --> 00:37:55.806
I wanted him to come and live with us.

00:37:55.866 --> 00:38:01.408
But he is too old now, and he went away.

00:38:01.468 --> 00:38:05.126
I don't know where.

00:38:05.186 --> 00:38:13.350
Gertrude knew about this boy now, and all of Rhoda Brooke's story.

00:38:13.410 --> 00:38:18.596
But she and her husband never spoke about it.

00:38:18.656 --> 00:38:31.312
And she never said anything to him about her visit to the wise man of Eggedon Heath, or about the face in the glass.

00:38:31.372 --> 00:38:37.668
She wanted so much to find a cure for her arm.

00:38:37.728 --> 00:38:44.850
My husband cannot love me because of this arm, she thought.

00:38:44.910 --> 00:38:48.441
So I must find a cure for it.

00:38:48.501 --> 00:38:50.322
I must.

00:38:50.382 --> 00:38:54.373
The wise man helped me before.

00:38:54.433 --> 00:38:59.153
Perhaps he can help me again.

00:38:59.213 --> 00:39:06.184
So one day she walked to Eddyn Heath.

00:39:06.244 --> 00:39:14.928
She did not know the way, but at last she found the house.

00:39:14.988 --> 00:39:22.962
You can send away other things I know, she said, to Trendall.

00:39:23.022 --> 00:39:32.337
Hair on women's faces and things like that Why can't you send this away?"

00:39:32.397 --> 00:39:36.940
She uncovered her poor withered arm.

00:39:37.000 --> 00:39:43.614
No, I'm sorry, but I can't help you.

00:39:43.674 --> 00:39:45.984
Said Drenville.

00:39:46.044 --> 00:39:50.518
Your arm is withered because of a curse.

00:39:50.578 --> 00:39:55.527
It's not easy to find a cure for that.

00:39:55.588 --> 00:39:59.816
Is there no cure anywhere?"

00:39:59.876 --> 00:40:03.328
asked Gertrude sadly.

00:40:03.388 --> 00:40:06.969
There is one thing.

00:40:06.989 --> 00:40:11.281
Trandall began slowly.

00:40:11.341 --> 00:40:15.253
But it's not easy for a woman to do.

00:40:15.273 --> 00:40:22.732
Oh, tell me, said Gertrude, please.

00:40:22.792 --> 00:40:30.594
You must put the withered arm on the neck of a hanged man.

00:40:30.654 --> 00:40:40.774
You must do it before he's cold, just after they take his body down.

00:40:40.834 --> 00:40:45.368
Gertrude's face was pale.

00:40:45.428 --> 00:40:48.798
How can that do good?

00:40:48.858 --> 00:40:56.684
It can turn the blood, and that changes many things in the body.

00:40:56.744 --> 00:41:07.005
You must go to the jail when they hang someone and wait for the body when they bring it in.

00:41:07.065 --> 00:41:11.798
In the old days, lots of people did it.

00:41:11.859 --> 00:41:16.060
These days, not so many do it.

00:41:16.120 --> 00:41:21.954
But it is still the best cure for a curse.

00:41:22.014 --> 00:41:28.698
Back at home, Gertrude thought about this for a long time.

00:41:28.758 --> 00:41:32.220
She tried to forget it.

00:41:32.281 --> 00:41:34.522
But she couldn't.

00:41:34.582 --> 00:41:37.944
She wanted to be pretty again.

00:41:38.004 --> 00:41:42.508
She wanted her husband to love her again.

00:41:42.568 --> 00:41:47.172
Yes, she must try this cure.

00:41:47.232 --> 00:41:49.112
She must.

00:41:49.172 --> 00:41:52.014
But how do I do it?

00:41:52.074 --> 00:41:53.755
She thought.

00:41:53.815 --> 00:41:57.306
Where is the nearest jail?

00:41:57.366 --> 00:42:00.188
How can I get there?

00:42:00.248 --> 00:42:04.270
How often do they hang people?

00:42:04.330 --> 00:42:13.305
And when there is a hanging, how can I learn about it before it happens?

00:42:13.365 --> 00:42:16.866
so many questions.

00:42:16.926 --> 00:42:24.719
There was no one to help her, but slowly she began to find the answers.

00:42:24.780 --> 00:42:34.512
She asked careful questions in the village because country people always know everything.

00:42:34.572 --> 00:42:38.784
One old man was very helpful.

00:42:38.844 --> 00:42:43.794
The nearest jail is a caster bridge.

00:42:43.854 --> 00:42:49.396
Fifteen miles away he told Gertrude.

00:42:49.456 --> 00:42:59.963
They have trials there every three months and there's usually a hanging after the trials.

00:43:00.023 --> 00:43:11.502
Some poor man or boy takes a cow or a sheep or just some bread and they hang him for it.

00:43:11.562 --> 00:43:15.015
Lots of people go to watch the hangings.

00:43:15.075 --> 00:43:16.616
I don't know why.

00:43:16.636 --> 00:43:23.098
The next trials were in July, Gertrude learned.

00:43:23.158 --> 00:43:29.690
She asked her husband about them, but Lodge said very little.

00:43:29.750 --> 00:43:36.333
He was colder to her than usual, and she did not ask him again.

00:43:36.394 --> 00:43:43.166
He was often away these days, so she did not see much of him.

00:43:43.226 --> 00:43:50.857
July came, and Gertrude went to see the helpful old man in the village again.

00:43:50.917 --> 00:43:55.738
Just one hanging this time, he told her.

00:43:55.798 --> 00:44:03.270
It's for Arson, I think, they're going to hang him next Saturday.

00:44:03.330 --> 00:44:07.471
Gertrude walked slowly home.

00:44:07.532 --> 00:44:15.228
cannot tell my husband about this, this cure, she thought.

00:44:15.288 --> 00:44:21.152
And how can I be away from home for two nights?

00:44:21.212 --> 00:44:24.484
What can I say to him?

00:44:24.544 --> 00:44:28.616
But in the end, it was easy.

00:44:28.676 --> 00:44:34.466
On the Thursday before the hanging, Lodge came to her.

00:44:34.526 --> 00:44:41.004
I'm going away for three nights," he said.

00:44:41.064 --> 00:44:46.045
It's about farm work, so you can't come with me.

00:44:46.106 --> 00:44:51.197
That's all right, Gertrude said quietly.

00:44:51.257 --> 00:44:54.968
I'm happy to stay at home.

00:44:55.028 --> 00:44:58.270
They said nothing more.

00:44:58.330 --> 00:45:12.803
And on Thursday, Lodge drove away in the carriage.

00:45:12.863 --> 00:45:33.750
Chapter 5 The Hangman The next morning Gertrude got ready to leave the caster bridge.

00:45:33.810 --> 00:45:51.192
She did not want to go by road, because she did not want to meet any of her husband's friends So she took one of the heavy horses from the farm and rode west across the hills.

00:45:51.252 --> 00:46:02.453
She was afraid of riding with a half-dead arm, but the farm horse was quiet and slow and easy to ride.

00:46:02.513 --> 00:46:13.846
He carried her uphill and downhill, past rivers and through trees, moving west all the time.

00:46:13.906 --> 00:46:27.518
The sun slowly went down in the sky, and it was nearly eight o'clock when Gertrude stopped for a moment at the top of a hill.

00:46:27.578 --> 00:46:37.506
It was the last hill before the town, and she could see the roofs of Castabridge below.

00:46:37.566 --> 00:46:49.827
There was a big building on a hill at the end of the town, with a white roof She knew this was the jail.

00:46:49.887 --> 00:46:55.212
And she could see a lot of workmen on the roof.

00:46:55.272 --> 00:46:57.905
What are they doing?

00:46:57.965 --> 00:46:59.646
She thought.

00:46:59.706 --> 00:47:05.244
They're building something up there on the roof.

00:47:05.304 --> 00:47:12.650
Suddenly she understood, and quickly turned her eyes away.

00:47:12.710 --> 00:47:18.723
It was a warm summer evening, but she shivered with cold.

00:47:18.783 --> 00:47:24.106
Tomorrow they're going to hang a man on that roof.

00:47:24.166 --> 00:47:30.881
She thought, and when he is dead, she shivered again.

00:47:30.941 --> 00:47:43.060
But then she remembered her husband's cold words and his unsmiling face and she rode on down into the town.

00:47:43.120 --> 00:47:50.146
She found a room to stay for the night and then went out into the town.

00:47:50.206 --> 00:47:52.818
What do I do now?

00:47:52.878 --> 00:47:58.422
She thought, how can I get into the jail tomorrow?

00:47:58.482 --> 00:48:01.082
Who must I talk to?

00:48:01.142 --> 00:48:06.442
the men at the jail or the hangman.

00:48:06.502 --> 00:48:13.835
She was afraid to go to the jail, so she went to find the hangman.

00:48:13.895 --> 00:48:20.368
He had a house down by the river, a boy in the town told her.

00:48:20.428 --> 00:48:30.004
When she found the house, she stood outside for some minutes, afraid to go to the door.

00:48:30.064 --> 00:48:36.211
Then the door opened, and a man came out.

00:48:36.271 --> 00:48:38.652
Who are you?

00:48:38.712 --> 00:48:42.505
He called out, what do you want?

00:48:42.565 --> 00:48:46.808
I want to speak to you for a minute.

00:48:46.868 --> 00:48:50.691
He came nearer and looked at her.

00:48:50.751 --> 00:48:57.346
Well, well, that's a pretty face, he said.

00:48:57.406 --> 00:49:00.344
Come into the house.

00:49:00.404 --> 00:49:03.522
They went inside.

00:49:03.582 --> 00:49:13.654
Davis, that was his name, was a hangman on some days, but a gardener on other days.

00:49:13.714 --> 00:49:17.875
Is it about gardening work?

00:49:17.935 --> 00:49:20.546
He asked Gertrude.

00:49:20.606 --> 00:49:25.871
I can't do any tomorrow because I'm working at the jail.

00:49:25.931 --> 00:49:29.218
Yes, yes I know.

00:49:29.278 --> 00:49:32.062
That's why I'm here.

00:49:32.122 --> 00:49:34.544
I thought so.

00:49:34.604 --> 00:49:37.628
Is the poor man one of your family then?

00:49:37.688 --> 00:49:40.652
Perhaps your young brother?

00:49:40.712 --> 00:49:42.435
No.

00:49:42.495 --> 00:49:46.078
Davis looked at Gertrude's dress.

00:49:46.138 --> 00:49:48.260
I don't think so.

00:49:48.320 --> 00:49:53.117
Was he one of your farm workers, perhaps?

00:49:53.177 --> 00:49:54.699
No.

00:49:54.759 --> 00:49:57.613
What time is the hanging?

00:49:57.673 --> 00:49:59.936
The same as usual.

00:49:59.996 --> 00:50:02.219
Twelve o'clock.

00:50:02.279 --> 00:50:04.409
And it is.

00:50:04.469 --> 00:50:07.308
It is going to happen.

00:50:07.368 --> 00:50:08.830
Yes?

00:50:08.890 --> 00:50:10.340
Oh, yes.

00:50:10.400 --> 00:50:13.282
Nothing can stop the hanging now.

00:50:13.342 --> 00:50:15.164
Said Davis.

00:50:15.224 --> 00:50:18.106
But I'm sorry for this young man.

00:50:18.166 --> 00:50:20.268
I truly am.

00:50:20.328 --> 00:50:22.618
He's only eighteen.

00:50:22.678 --> 00:50:24.910
They say it was arson.

00:50:24.970 --> 00:50:26.972
But I don't know.

00:50:27.032 --> 00:50:30.274
He was there when the fire began.

00:50:30.334 --> 00:50:33.416
But there were twenty other men there too.

00:50:33.476 --> 00:50:35.159
So how do they know?

00:50:35.220 --> 00:50:39.696
I think they just want to hang someone, anyone.

00:50:39.756 --> 00:50:44.000
But what can I do for you, my pretty?"

00:50:44.060 --> 00:50:48.804
I need a cure, Gertrude said.

00:50:48.864 --> 00:50:51.357
A cure for a curse.

00:50:51.417 --> 00:51:03.728
And a wise man told me about the hanged man, and—and turning the blood Oh, yes, Miss.

00:51:03.788 --> 00:51:05.979
Now I understand.

00:51:06.039 --> 00:51:09.010
People sometimes come for that.

00:51:09.070 --> 00:51:12.530
But not pretty young things like you.

00:51:12.591 --> 00:51:16.952
Well, well, what's the cure for?

00:51:17.012 --> 00:51:19.342
It's this.

00:51:19.402 --> 00:51:23.524
Gertrude uncovered her left arm.

00:51:23.584 --> 00:51:31.168
Ah, it's all withered, said the hangman, looking at it.

00:51:31.228 --> 00:51:34.194
Yes, she said.

00:51:34.254 --> 00:51:41.268
Well, a hanged man's neck is the best cure for that, he said.

00:51:41.328 --> 00:51:44.679
Your wise man was right.

00:51:44.740 --> 00:51:48.452
So, can you help me?

00:51:48.513 --> 00:51:51.103
Gertrude whispered.

00:51:51.164 --> 00:52:01.629
Usually people go to the jail and take their doctor with them and give their name and address.

00:52:01.689 --> 00:52:09.313
But yes, I can help you for a little money, perhaps.

00:52:09.374 --> 00:52:14.498
Oh, thank you, Gertrude said.

00:52:14.558 --> 00:52:16.900
It's better like this.

00:52:16.960 --> 00:52:20.254
I don't want people to know about it.

00:52:20.314 --> 00:52:24.056
Don't want your lover to know, eh?

00:52:24.116 --> 00:52:27.219
No, husband.

00:52:27.279 --> 00:52:29.060
Uh-huh.

00:52:29.120 --> 00:52:30.970
Very well.

00:52:31.031 --> 00:52:34.382
You can touch the body.

00:52:34.442 --> 00:52:37.574
Where is it now?

00:52:37.634 --> 00:52:40.514
She said, shivering.

00:52:40.574 --> 00:52:42.065
It?

00:52:42.125 --> 00:52:44.306
He, you mean?

00:52:44.366 --> 00:52:47.037
He's still alive tonight.

00:52:47.097 --> 00:52:52.779
He's in the jail, a little room right at the top.

00:52:52.840 --> 00:52:57.072
And what must I do tomorrow?

00:52:57.132 --> 00:52:59.425
Gertrude said.

00:52:59.485 --> 00:53:03.919
There's a little door at the back of the jail.

00:53:03.979 --> 00:53:06.609
Be there at one o'clock.

00:53:06.669 --> 00:53:09.030
No later.

00:53:09.090 --> 00:53:18.611
I can open the door from inside and can take you to the body when they bring him in.

00:53:18.671 --> 00:53:20.342
Good night.

00:53:20.402 --> 00:53:22.142
Don't be late.

00:53:22.202 --> 00:53:25.202
And you don't want people to see you.

00:53:25.262 --> 00:53:27.493
So cover your face.

00:53:27.553 --> 00:53:30.788
Good night, my pretty.

00:53:30.848 --> 00:53:37.518
Gertrude went away and walked up to the jail on the hill.

00:53:37.578 --> 00:53:44.045
She wanted to find the little door at the back to know it for tomorrow.

00:53:44.105 --> 00:53:56.828
Then she went back down into the town and went to her room and waited for the morning.

00:53:56.888 --> 00:54:15.640
Chapter 6 The Blood Turns At half past twelve on Saturday, Gertrude Lodge walked up the hill to the jail.

00:54:15.700 --> 00:54:32.048
She went there by the small back streets because there were so many people in the town.

00:54:32.108 --> 00:54:37.924
They were there for a holiday to watch the hanging.

00:54:37.984 --> 00:54:43.539
At one o'clock she was inside the jail.

00:54:43.599 --> 00:54:49.467
The hangman took her to a long dark room with a table.

00:54:49.527 --> 00:54:53.362
Wait there, he told her.

00:54:53.422 --> 00:54:57.556
Two or three minutes, no more.

00:54:57.616 --> 00:55:03.270
He went away and Gertrude waited.

00:55:03.330 --> 00:55:11.326
She had a veil over her face and her left arm was uncovered, ready.

00:55:11.386 --> 00:55:21.156
She stood still with her eyes closed, listening and shivering with terror.

00:55:21.216 --> 00:55:29.135
Soon she heard noises and could hear heavy feet on the stairs.

00:55:29.195 --> 00:55:39.084
The heavy feet came nearer, and four men came into the room with a long box.

00:55:39.144 --> 00:55:49.993
It was open, and in it was the body of a young man, with a cover over his face.

00:55:50.053 --> 00:55:54.274
The men put the box down on the table.

00:55:54.334 --> 00:55:59.126
Now said a voice in Gertrude's ear.

00:55:59.186 --> 00:56:00.976
Now!

00:56:01.036 --> 00:56:06.188
But the young woman was half dead with terror.

00:56:06.248 --> 00:56:10.790
And at first she could not move.

00:56:10.850 --> 00:56:18.242
Then she opened her eyes and came up to the table.

00:56:18.302 --> 00:56:27.148
She could hear other noises outside the room, and there were more people coming.

00:56:27.208 --> 00:56:32.822
Davis, the hangman, was by her side.

00:56:32.882 --> 00:56:44.398
He uncovered the body's face, took Gertrude's hand, and put her arm across the dead man's neck.

00:56:44.458 --> 00:56:47.886
Gertrude screamed.

00:56:47.946 --> 00:56:53.008
And at once there was a second scream.

00:56:53.068 --> 00:56:58.370
A woman's scream, but not Gertrude's.

00:56:58.430 --> 00:57:02.162
Gertrude turned round.

00:57:02.223 --> 00:57:12.407
Behind her stood Rhoda Brooke, her face pale, and her eyes red with crying.

00:57:12.467 --> 00:57:18.171
Behind Rhoda stood Gertrude's husband.

00:57:18.231 --> 00:57:27.088
He looked old and sad, but there were no tears in his eyes.

00:57:27.148 --> 00:57:29.240
You!

00:57:29.300 --> 00:57:34.414
What in God's name are you doing here?

00:57:34.475 --> 00:57:40.524
He whispered angrily.

00:57:40.584 --> 00:57:49.596
Why do you come between us and our child now?

00:57:49.656 --> 00:57:53.900
This is the true meaning of my dream.

00:57:53.960 --> 00:58:00.184
You are like that cruel phantom at last.

00:58:00.244 --> 00:58:12.878
When Gertrude saw her husband with Rhoda, she knew at once that the dead young man was Rhoda's son.

00:58:12.938 --> 00:58:19.162
She stared at Rhoda, with terror in her eyes.

00:58:19.223 --> 00:58:30.926
Then Rhoda ran to Gertrude, closed her hand round the younger woman's arm and pulled her away from the table.

00:58:30.986 --> 00:58:40.813
When she let go of the arm, the young wife fell down at her husband's feet.

00:58:40.873 --> 00:58:46.030
She never opened her eyes again.

00:58:46.091 --> 00:58:51.944
They carried her out of the jail into the town.

00:58:52.004 --> 00:58:56.186
But she never got home alive.

00:58:56.246 --> 00:59:01.720
Perhaps it was the turning of the blood.

00:59:01.780 --> 00:59:06.851
Perhaps it was her withered arm.

00:59:06.911 --> 00:59:17.332
Perhaps it was her terror in the jail when she turned and saw Rhoda behind her.

00:59:17.393 --> 00:59:26.114
Doctors came and looked at her, but they could do nothing to help her.

00:59:26.174 --> 00:59:31.713
And three days later she died.

00:59:31.773 --> 00:59:43.356
In those days, the unhappy parents of a hanged man came and took the body away after the hanging.

00:59:43.416 --> 00:59:51.026
That was why Farmer Lodge was at the jail with Rhoda that day.

00:59:51.086 --> 00:59:56.665
It was not his first visit to the jail.

00:59:56.726 --> 01:00:04.058
With Rhoda, he went many times to visit his son that summer.

01:00:04.118 --> 01:00:11.022
And that was why he was away from the farm so often.

01:00:11.082 --> 01:00:22.212
But after his young wife died, nobody ever saw Farmer Lodge in Casterbridge again.

01:00:22.272 --> 01:00:29.231
He went home to his farm, but he did not stay there long.

01:00:29.291 --> 01:00:40.898
After a short time, he sold the farm and the farmhouse and all the cows and sheep and horses.

01:00:40.958 --> 01:00:47.700
Then he went away to live in a small town by the sea.

01:00:47.760 --> 01:00:55.352
He lived very quietly, without any friends or family near him.

01:00:55.412 --> 01:01:02.346
When he died, two years later, he left a lot of money.

01:01:02.406 --> 01:01:07.300
Most of it went to a home for poor boys.

01:01:07.360 --> 01:01:12.013
But there was money for Rhoda Brooke too.

01:01:12.073 --> 01:01:17.969
For some time, nobody could find Rhoda.

01:01:18.030 --> 01:01:25.449
Then one day she came back to her old house near the dairy.

01:01:25.509 --> 01:01:31.754
But she never took a penny of farmer lodges money.

01:01:31.814 --> 01:01:46.952
She went back to work in the dairy and worked there for many long years, milking the cows in the morning and again in the evening.

01:01:47.013 --> 01:01:57.799
Her dark hair turned white and her sad pale face looked thin and old.

01:01:57.860 --> 01:02:07.351
Most people knew Rhoda's story and sometimes they watched her at milking time.

01:02:07.412 --> 01:02:17.432
What did she think about all those long days at morning and evening milking?

01:02:17.492 --> 01:02:21.246
But nobody ever asked her.

01:02:21.306 --> 01:02:25.171
And nobody ever knew the answer.

